        ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)={sin}^{4}\u2061(x),$ we have\n\n${f}^{\u2032}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we express\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x))^{4}.\n$$\n\nNow, we see that $f(x)$ can be expressed as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={u}^{4},\\,u=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x).\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=4{u}^{3},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x).\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =4{u}^{3}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x) \\\\  & =4{sin}^{3}\u2061(x)\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
